This pull request introduces significant changes to the deployment workflow and Lambda function structure, focusing on expanding environment support, simplifying deployment logic, and adding a new Lambda for policy graph ingestion. The main highlights include support for a new perf environment, removal of incremental deployment logic in favor of always deploying all Lambdas, and the addition of a new, database-integrated Lambda function with supporting code and configuration. Several legacy/sample Lambdas have been removed to streamline the repository.

Deployment workflow improvements:

Added support for a new perf environment in both workflow dispatch and automatic deployments based on branch name. [1] [2]
Simplified Lambda deployment logic to always deploy all Lambdas, removing the incremental change detection mechanism that relied on previous deployment state.
Updated the deployment workflow to use secrets.ARTIFACT_ROLE instead of vars.ARTIFACT_ROLE for improved security.
Removed the apigw-redeploy job from the workflow, as API Gateway redeployment is no longer handled here.
Lambda and configuration changes:

Added a new policy_graph_ingest Lambda, including handler, requirements, and a modular, testable codebase for ingesting and saving policy graph data to the database. This includes the main handler, a line-of-business mapper dispatch system, and a commercial auto payload mapper with robust logging and error handling. [1] [2] [3] [4] [5]
Updated config/environments.yml to support multiple API Gateway stages per environment and to add the perf environment.
Updated config/lambdas.yml to remove sample/example Lambdas and add configuration for the new policy_graph_ingest and soap_verification Lambdas, including environment-specific function names.
Removed the legacy example_hello Lambda and its code, further cleaning up unused sample code. [1] [2]
These changes collectively improve deployment reliability, environment flexibility, and introduce a production-ready Lambda for ingesting policy graph data.

